## Peg solitaire (peg-solitaire-r), generated from the Rosie teaching script (english-input.txt) under the world conventions.
##
## Instructor statements used (numbers as in english-input.txt):
##   4. If a peg is between a clear location and a block then you can remove the peg plus move the block onto the clear location.
##   5. If a location is not below an object then it is clear.
##   6. If an object is a block then it is a peg.
##  11. The goal is that the number of covered locations is one.
##  12. If a location is below an object then it is covered.
## World: init-pegr.world (a triangle of ten locations, nine pegs)
##
## Translation (tools/rosie-language.md gives the general reading; the assumption ledger is in README.md):
##   - Operator jump (argument1 = the jumping block, argument2 = the clear location), statement 4; every block is a peg
##     (statement 6). "between" needs the three locations in a line: step-1..8 static relations from the locations' x and y,
##     in the four directions and the two diagonals, one proposal per direction (A-G2, A-P6). clear is a maintained one-argument relation (statement 5).
##   - The jumped peg is removed: it loses its on relation and is off the board (A-P1).
##   - Goal (statement 11): one covered location: a covered location and no other (A-P2). "The solution has eight steps"
##     (statement 7) is checked against the plans, not used.

## Propose initialize-peg-solitaire-r when its conditions below hold.
sp {peg-solitaire-r*propose*initialize-peg-solitaire-r
   (state <s> ^superstate nil ^world <w> -^name)
-->
   (<s> ^operator <o> + >)
   (<o> ^name initialize-peg-solitaire-r ^task-operator false)
}

sp {peg-solitaire-r*apply*initialize-peg-solitaire-r
   (state <s> ^operator.name initialize-peg-solitaire-r ^world <w>)
   (<w> ^objects <objs>)
-->
   (<s> ^name peg-solitaire-r ^desireds <ds>)
   (<objs> ^object <o-location-1> <o-location-2> <o-location-3> <o-location-4> <o-location-5> <o-location-6> <o-location-7> <o-location-8> <o-location-9> <o-location-10> <o-block-11> <o-block-12> <o-block-13> <o-block-14> <o-block-15> <o-block-16> <o-block-17> <o-block-18> <o-block-19> <o-task>)
   (<o-location-1> ^object-handle location-1 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 1 ^y 1)
   (<o-location-2> ^object-handle location-2 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 2 ^y 1)
   (<o-location-3> ^object-handle location-3 ^anchored true ^type location ^x 3 ^y 1)
